<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="How time is recorded">
        <FluentText>
            Staff clock in and out on a clock-in terminal, with their PIN or by scanning its QR code. They can
            clock in from the clock-in window before a published shift at that location. You can also add
            time by hand.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Checking and approving">
        <ol>
            <li>Open <a href="/manage/rota/timesheets">Timesheets</a> and choose the week.</li>
            <li>Each person's days show the rota shift next to the clocked time, with any difference.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Approve</strong> on an entry, or <strong>Approve N ready</strong> to approve every
                finished entry that isn't flagged.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>Entries are flagged for review when, for example:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>nobody clocked out, so the entry was closed automatically after 16 hours;</li>
            <li>someone clocked in at one location and out at another.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>Check flagged entries and fix them before approving.</FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Adding or correcting time">
        <FluentText>
            Use <strong>Add time</strong> for cover shifts and forgotten clock-ins, or the edit button on an entry
            to correct it. Saving counts as your approval, except for your own time, which another manager or
            an admin approves. Entries can't overlap, be in the future or be longer than 24 hours.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Exporting for payroll">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Export</strong>.</li>
            <li>Choose <strong>Last pay period</strong> or <strong>This pay period</strong> (once your pay period
                is set in Rota Settings), <strong>This week</strong>, <strong>Last week</strong>, or your own dates.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Download CSV</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            The file has one row per person per day of approved hours, plus a total for each person. Time that
            isn't approved yet is listed as Excluded rows and not counted, so approve or fix it first if it
            should be paid this time.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
